            "title": "Coastal Plains of India: Submergent West vs Emergent East",
            "summary": "",
            "theoryHtml": "\n            <p>Flanking the Peninsular Plateau on either side are two narrow coastal strips: the <strong>Western Coastal Plain</strong> facing the Arabian Sea and the <strong>Eastern Coastal Plain</strong> facing the Bay of Bengal. Their fundamental geomorphic characteristics reflect contrasting tectonic histories of <strong>submergence versus emergence</strong>.</p>\n\n            <h4>1. Comparative Morphotectonic Analysis</h4>\n            <table class=\"table table-bordered\">\n                <thead>\n                    <tr><th>Parameter</th><th>Western Coastal Plain</th><th>Eastern Coastal Plain</th></tr>\n                </thead>\n                <tbody>\n                    <tr><td><strong>Tectonic Nature</strong></td><td>Predominantly <strong>Submergent Coast</strong> (drowned coast formed by downfaulting of the continental margin).</td><td>Predominantly <strong>Emergent Coast</strong> (uplifted continental shelf supplemented by massive sedimentation).</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td><strong>Width</strong></td><td>Narrow ($10\text{ to }50\text{ km}$ wide; broad only near Gujarat/Narmada mouth).</td><td>Wide and expansive ($80\text{ to }150\text{ km}$ wide).</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td><strong>River Terminus</strong></td><td>Rivers form <strong>Estuaries</strong> (Narmada, Tapti, Mandovi); deltas are absent.</td><td>Rivers construct massive prograding <strong>Deltas</strong> (Mahanadi, Godavari, Krishna, Kaveri).</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td><strong>Coastal Slope</strong></td><td>Steep offshore bathymetry; deep water close to shoreline.</td><td>Very gentle offshore gradient; shallow continental shelf.</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td><strong>Port Development</strong></td><td>Ideal for <strong>Natural Harbors & Deep-Water Ports</strong> (Mumbai, Nhava Sheva, Mormugao, Karwar, Kochi).</td><td>Requires dredging and construction of <strong>Artificial Harbors</strong> (Chennai, Visakhapatnam is landlocked, Tuticorin).</td></tr>\n                    <tr><td><strong>Lagoons & Lakes</strong></td><td>Backwaters and Kayals (Vembanad, Ashtamudi) behind offshore sandspits.</td><td>Large coastal lagoons and barrier spits (Chilika Lake, Pulicat Lake, Kolleru Lake).</td></tr>\n                </tbody>\n            </table>\n\n            <h4>2. Geomorphic Evolution</h4>\n            <p>The down-faulting of the western continental shelf during the Late Cretaceous and Tertiary drowned river valleys, giving rise to ria-like estuaries and rocky headlands (Konkan coast). Conversely, the eastern coast witnessed continuous progradation as massive volumes of alluvium from the Peninsular rivers built outward into the shallow shelf of the Bay of Bengal.</p>\n        ",
